hority.\n2|\n3|Verify with your own instruments: (1) Section 2.4 fixtures — for each of the seven normative fixtures (PROFILE-DIRECT-TAKEOVER/RESUME/FORK, PROFILE-TB-TAKEOVER/RESUME/FORK, PROFILE-PI-EQUAL-MAPPING) reconstruct the P0/E1/C1 scenario yourself through the production entries (Derive/DeriveForHeads, BundlePair, ForkProjection, FinalizePair, Check* pairs) over a real sessrepo chain and assert the exact required authority pairs (P1/E1, P1/null, source_profile_event_id=E1); confirm a losing-lease profile.changed and an ambiguous event never change the effective profile, that a closure containing E1 never falls back to P0, and that P0-after-C1, missing E1 and an inconsistent bundle profile refuse integrity_failure. (2) SetProfile transaction — drive Transactor.SetProfile: happy path appends exactly one profile.changed under the current lease; from == to refused; yolo without confirmation refused; stale epoch, divergent token and greater-epoch acting lease refused; retry with the identical request envelope replays the committed event without a second append (assert the chain length and bytes); a retry with a changed envelope member is refused or appends a distinct event — state which and why per the pinned text; crash injection between mint and append leaves no partial event admitted (rerun the producer's crash_test twice and add your own seam). (3) Section 7.7 mapping — extract the table yourself and diff against provhost.ResolveMapping/ProjectLaunchArgv: exact flags for Codex/Claude/Gemini/Muse/Antigravity, Pi 0.73.1 default_unrestricted_tool_set report-only with the equivalence disclosed, the codex `--yolo` alias refused for persistence, standard emitting no unrestricted flag and refusing a machine-local alias, exact-version probe required before mapping, an absent or changed flag failing closed, profile_mapping_unavailable exit 6 with provider/version/profile details registered through internal/axerror (confirm it is a legitimate registered class and no other new class was minted); plant your own inputs: a provider version one patch off the pinned Pi version, a base argv that already contains the unrestricted flag, a foreign provider's flag, an argv exceeding the Section 5.1 bounds by one. (4) Refusal census — the producer claims 12 new derived arms, floor 217 -> 229, seventh constructor; enumerate the arms of sessprofile and profile_resolve.go, attack the witness instrument (swap two adjacent arms sharing a code; one-token swallow; delete one arm) and confirm the suite goes RED for each; report n-of-m with call sites. (5) Mutation — rerun testdata/mutate_profile.py in an isolated copy, rerun each of the 20 KILLED twice, plant at least four narrowing mutants of your own on arms the producer did not mutate (closure membership check widened by one event; lease/sequence order compare `<=`; equivalence disclosure dropped for Pi; confirmation check skipped when from is yolo) plus an applied harmless SURVIVED control; per-plant raw logs, subprocess exits, precise denominators. (6) Bounds — B1 (no named profile registry in the pinned text) verified by grep over SPEC.v0.6.0.md; the no-attestation-outside-the-leaf bound (CalculateObjectIdentity, never Verify) censused; the secprim unrestrictedTokens census row is a true one-language registration; no traceability row touched (final-leaf owned — confirm the Story's final leaf brief will have to carry section:2.4/7.7 bindings and say so). (7) Docs and hygiene — README package section and LOGBOOK make no CLI/capability claim (no ax start/set-profile command exists); changed_paths exactly the candidate paths, no __pycache__/.pyc, no task-board.config.json, no stray plants; gofmt/vet clean; go test ./internal/sessprofile ./internal/provhost ./internal/sessrepo ./internal/secprim -count=1 and -race green; tracecheck and cataloggen -check exit 0 on the exact tree.\n4|\n5|Method: isolated immutable probes only, never mutate the live Story worktree, index, branch or HEAD; no product edits, commits, checkpoints or integration; Curator go-testing-tools skill; all CI local; PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 for every harness; keep scratch small under .temp/TASK-260830-3uzfyn/ and delete candidate copies when done. Attach TASK-260830-3uzfyn_review-verdict-rev1.md and TASK-260830-3uzfyn_review-evidence-rev1.tar.gz (a real gzip archive), complete the live merged checklist, then accept_cr(TASK-260830-3uzfyn, revision=1, evidence=TASK-260830-3uzfyn_review-verdict-rev1.md) or hand off changes requested with P1/P2/P3 classes named. Model: muse-spark xhigh (codex reviewers are out of quota until 2026-09-19). Canonical CLI /Users/iv/.curator/global/bin/task-board.","final_result":true}}}
