n value when the closure holds a later change; fork projects the source-checkpoint effective profile as the new Session Record creation profile with profile_source_event_id null and fork.created.source_profile_event_id as provenance only; ax session set-profile appends a new event under the current lease with operator confirmation when changing to yolo; the seven normative fixtures PROFILE-DIRECT-TAKEOVER/RESUME/FORK, PROFILE-TB-TAKEOVER/RESUME/FORK, PROFILE-PI-EQUAL-MAPPING; integrity_failure for P0-after-C1, missing E1, or a bundle profile inconsistent with C1) and Section 7.7 Profile mapping (per-provider yolo flags, standard omits every unrestricted flag and never reuses a machine-local alias, Pi 0.73.1 default_unrestricted_tool_set disclosure, exact-version probe before applying a mapping, absent/changed flag fails closed, profile_mapping_unavailable on resume when the adapter cannot map the stored profile for the probed version), with Sections 5.5 and 8 (provider identity record, capability/platform matrix) as the tuple authority. Deliver as production code over the landed owners without forking a second model: (a) the effective-profile derivation as a pure reducer beside internal/sessstate (its doc.go records that Section 2.4 derivation was out of the earlier leaf's scope — that gap is yours: derive from the validated Session Record and the authoritative event chain sessstate already orders, driving the landed lease/authority admission rather than re-implementing it), exposing effective profile + profile_source_event_id for a session head and for a checkpoint's event-head closure (use the landed internal/sessckpt closure or sessquery admission if it gives you the closure; otherwise define the closure input explicitly and say so); (b) the profile.changed transaction (set-profile) as an event appended under the current lease through the landed internal/sessrepo append/attest path with a confirmation requirement for yolo, idempotent on retry, refused for a losing or expired lease, refused when from == to; (c) the provider mapping table of Section 7.7 as data plus the mapping resolver that requires an exact-version probe result (reuse internal/provhost identity/tuple verification from kp4zpu) and refuses profile_mapping_unavailable / an absent or changed flag / a machine-local alias; the sanitized launch-plan projection that emits the unrestricted flag only for yolo and discloses the Pi equivalence; (d) the projections the fixtures require (bundle projection, plugin resume pair, resumed/fork event pairs) at the reducer/record level — do not implement takeover/resume/fork transactions themselves (owned elsewhere); (e) no separate \"named profile registry\" or CLI unless the pinned spec defines one — if you find none, say so in the results and the LOGBOOK; no ax command surface is added. Tests: the seven Section 2.4 fixtures driven end to end at the record/reducer level with exact P0/E1/C1 assertions; negatives for losing-lease and ambiguous profile.changed events, P0-after-C1, missing E1, inconsistent bundle profile, from == to, unconfirmed yolo, expired/losing lease at set-profile, unmapped provider version, changed flag, alias reuse, standard emitting an unrestricted flag; crash/idempotency evidence for the set-profile append (interrupted append leaves no partial event admitted; retry idempotent); narrowing mutants per refusal with a shipped harness and an applied harmless SURVIVED control; conformance matrix mapping each Section 2.4/7.7 clause to a test or a stated bound. Update README (package section with test commands, no capability claim) and LOGBOOK; do not touch internal/traceability ownership rows (the Story's final leaf carries the registry update and digest re-pin). Managed Story worktree contract: .temp/STORY-260830-315721/worktree on branch task-board/story/STORY-260830-315721 whose tip is the kp4zpu checkpoint; leave the candidate UNCOMMITTED, never commit on the Story branch, never edit .task-board directly, 