{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c5c9","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ae27-7230-7e51-8e87-49c1be7949af"},"sequence":319,"recorded_at":1780531400000633,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"55e4c923-a9c7-4adf-b93d-01f4daa5924d","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"55e4c923-a9c7-4adf-b93d-01f4daa5924d","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"55e4c923-a9c7-4adf-b93d-01f4daa5924d"},"call_id":"call_01a0ae28940772d593bfad427c7be3bf","text":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260830-3uzfyn/TASK-260830-3uzfyn_reviewer-cr1.md`.\n1|Independently review Change Request revision 1 of TASK-260830-3uzfyn (implement-profile-resolution-and-persistence, second leaf of STORY-260830-315721 provider-identity-profile-and-resume after the checkpointed kp4zpu provider-identity leaf; sibling 2zvo8m native resume smoke framework follows; task_delta on the Story branch (trunk base 62d446304391af187c417a88a2e14012b467956e; checkpointed predecessors 736955a ; tip 736955aa621143d73c9317c9ef81247987970ad4), published by RUN-260917-0605fd on muse-spark max, 24 changed paths, patch and validation log attached as TASK-260830-3uzfyn_change-request_rev1.patch / _rev1-validation.log). Read the producer brief TASK-260830-3uzfyn_producer.md, the outcome TASK-260830-3uzfyn_results.md, TASK-260830-3uzfyn_conformance-matrix.md (16 rows, bounds B1-B8), TASK-260830-3uzfyn_producer-evidence.tar.gz (mutants.json + per-plant logs, full/race/cover logs, digests), the CR patch and validation log, and the exact immutable CR bytes. The normative authority is the pinned internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md Section 2.4 Execution profiles and Section 7.7 Profile mapping with Sections 5.5/8 as tuple authority.\n2|\n3|Verify with your own instruments: (1) Section 2.4 fixtures — for each of the seven normative fixtures (PROFILE-DIRECT-TAKEOVER/RESUME/FORK, PROFILE-TB-TAKEOVER/RESUME/FORK, PROFILE-PI-EQUAL-MAPPING) reconstruct the P0/E1/C1 scenario yourself through the production entries (Derive/DeriveForHeads, BundlePair, ForkProjection, FinalizePair, Check* pairs) over a real sessrepo chain and assert the exact required authority pairs (P1/E1, P1/null, source_profile_event_id=E1); confirm a losing-lease profile.changed and an ambiguous event never change the effective profile, that a closure containing E1 never falls back to P0, and that P0-after-C1, missing E1 and an inconsistent bundle profile refuse integrity_failure. (2) SetProfile transaction — drive Transactor.SetProfile: happy path appends exactly one profile.changed under the current lease; from == to refused; yolo without confirmation refused; stale epoch, divergent token and greater-epoch acting lease refused; retry with the identical request envelope replays the committed event without a second append (assert the chain length and bytes); a retry with a changed envelope member is refused or appends a distinct event — state which and why per the pinned text; crash injection between mint and append leaves no partial event admitted (rerun the producer's crash_test twice and add your own seam). (3) Section 7.7 mapping — extract the table yourself and diff against provhost.ResolveMapping/ProjectLaunchArgv: exact flags for Codex/Claude/Gemini/Muse/Antigravity, Pi 0.73.1 default_unrestricted_tool_set report-only with the equivalence disclosed, the codex `--yolo` alias refused for persistence, standard emitting no unrestricted flag and refusing a machine-local alias, exact-version probe required before mapping, an absent or changed flag failing closed, profile_mapping_unavailable exit 6 with provider/version/profile details registered through internal/axerror (confirm it is a legitimate registered class and no other new class was minted); plant your own inputs: a provider version one patch off the pinned Pi version, a base argv that already contains the unrestricted flag